{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Paccaya","html":"<article id='thag3.2'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 3.2 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 3.2 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tikanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Threes </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Paccayattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Paccaya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Pañcāhāhaṁ pabbajito, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I went forth five days ago, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sekho appattamānaso; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a trainee, my heart’s desire unfulfilled. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vihāraṁ me paviṭṭhassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I entered my dwelling </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cetaso paṇidhī ahu. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and resolved in my heart: </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nāsissaṁ na pivissāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I won’t eat; I won’t drink; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vihārato na nikkhame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I won’t leave my dwelling; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Napi passaṁ nipātessaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor will I lie down on my side—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>taṇhāsalle anūhate. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>not until the dart of craving is plucked. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tassa mevaṁ viharato, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>See my energy and vigor </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>passa vīriyaparakkamaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as I meditate like this! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tisso vijjā anuppattā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ve attained the three knowledges </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kataṁ buddhassa sāsanan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and fulfilled the Buddha’s instructions. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Paccayo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
